Mipmapping: pre-calculated progressively smaller versions of texture stored alongside original (reduces aliasing)
Tessellation: dynamically subdivide coarse polygons into finer triangles
Level of detail (LOD): lower complexity representation for objects far from camera
Signed distance function (SDF): resolution independent smooth rendering based on mathematical function (expensive close to camera)

=Texture mapping:
Bump mapping: illusion of bumps and wrinkles by perturbing surface normals
Parallax mapping: bump mapping extension, shift UV coordinates based on heightmap and viewing angle (add depth to flat surfaces)
